SUPPLEMENTARY MATERIAL

to the work

Global approximation to the Boys functions for vectorized computation

by

Dimitri N. Laikov

FILE       DESCRIPTION

makefile   Data file for UNIX make utility used to compile the code.

t_fn.c     C code, main file.

t_fpn.c    C code, mathematical functions,
           one source to be converted on-the-fly to 4 floating-point data types.

c0n4.c     Coefficients c_n of Eq. (3), and z_nb of Eq. (17).

cnm4.c     Approximation coefficients for the rational function of Eq. (11), polynomial.

z0nm4.c    Approximation coefficients in terms of polynomial roots.

z1nm4.c    Approximation coefficients in terms of polynomial roots as in Eqs. (12), (13), (14).

RUNNING THE CODE

What the code does can be learnt from it, thanks to C.
But to soften the experience, here is an example
with all command line arguments followed by short explanation:

./t_fn L:4 z:2 f:50 c:0 t:2 p:-1,0 b:12 x: r:z o:0

L:4     sets the order n = 4 of the function computed by the approximation,
        followed by the recursion down to m = 0.

z:0     compute polynomials directly from their coefficients.
z:1     compute polynomials in terms of their roots, but without the polynomial division.
z:2     compute polynomials in terms of their roots, as in Eqs. (12), (13), (14).
z:3     compute polynomials in terms of positive-real-part roots and one more polynomial.

f:50    select the approximation accurate to at least 50 bits.
f:0     use the infinite series summation, asymptotic formula for large argument.

c:0     use the above selection.
c:4     use the approximation of order N = 4.
c:-1    use the approximation for the single precision as in Table 1.
c:-2    use the approximation for the double precision as in Table 1.
c:-3    use the approximation for the current precision if it is single or double.

t:1     use single          precision, "float"       data type.
t:2     use double          precision, "double"      data type.
t:3     use double extended precision, "long double" data type.
t:4     use quadruple       precision, "__float128"  data type.

p:-1,0  binary exponent range for the argument from -1 to 0 (see the source code).

b:12    run through all 12-bit values of mantissa (see the source code).

x:      scale the above values by the z_nb of Eq. (17),
        otherwise take them as they are.

r:z     set the rounding mode to round-to-zero.

o:0     do not print each value, only the maximum errors for m = 0, ..., n .
o:1     print all the values (may need output redirection to a file),
        can be used for plotting.

